skinparam shadowing false
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam participantPadding 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 80

' ------------------------------------------------------------
' Diagram 1: 5G Signaling: AS vs NAS
' ------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml 5G_AS_vs_NAS
title 5G Signaling: Access Stratum (AS) vs Non-Access Stratum (NAS)

actor UE
participant "gNB\n(5G Base Station)" as gNB
participant "AMF\n(Core Control Plane)" as AMF

== Access Stratum (AS) - Radio Control ==
UE -> gNB: RRC Setup Request
gNB -> UE: RRC Setup
UE -> gNB: RRC Setup Complete

note right of gNB
AS = UE <-> gNB
Radio Access Control
Examples: RRC, PDCP, RLC, MAC
end note

== NAS messages are carried inside AS ==
UE -> gNB: NAS: Registration Request\n(encapsulated inside RRC/N2 transport)
gNB -> AMF: Forward NAS via N2\n(Initial UE Message)

note right of AMF
NAS = UE <-> AMF
Core Control Messaging
Examples:
- Registration
- Authentication (5G-AKA)
- NAS Security Mode
- Mobility updates
end note

== NAS Authentication Example ==
AMF -> gNB: NAS: Authentication Request
gNB -> UE: NAS: Authentication Request

UE -> gNB: NAS: Authentication Response
gNB -> AMF: NAS: Authentication Response

== After Security Mode ==
AMF -> UE: NAS Security Mode Command\n(Integrity + Cipher)
UE -> AMF: NAS Security Mode Complete

note bottom
Key point:
NAS is logically UE<->AMF,
but physically it passes through gNB.

gNB does NOT process NAS contents;
it forwards it like a courier.
end note
@enduml


' ------------------------------------------------------------
' Diagram 2: 5G Control Plane vs User Plane (N2 vs N3)
' ------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml 5G_CP_vs_UP
title 5G: Control Plane vs User Plane (N2 vs N3)

actor UE
participant "gNB\n(5G Base Station)" as gNB
participant "AMF\n(Control Plane)" as AMF
participant "SMF\n(Session Control)" as SMF
participant "UPF\n(User Plane)" as UPF
participant "DN\n(Internet)" as DN

== CONTROL PLANE (Signaling) ==
note over UE,SMF
Control Plane is about setup and management:
- Registration
- 5G-AKA Authentication
- Security Mode
- PDU Session Establishment
end note

UE -> gNB: NAS: Registration Request
gNB -> AMF: N2: Initial UE Message\n(forwards NAS)

AMF -> SMF: SBA: Create Session Context\n(Nsmf_PDUSession...)
SMF -> UPF: N4: Configure forwarding rules\n(PDR/FAR/QER)

SMF --> AMF: Session Accepted\n(N2 SM info)
AMF -> gNB: N2: PDU Session Resource Setup Request
gNB -> AMF: N2: Resource Setup Response

AMF -> UE: NAS: PDU Session Establishment Accept\n(IP/QoS info)

== USER PLANE (Actual Data) ==
note over UE,DN
User Plane carries real traffic:
YouTube / WhatsApp / HTTP / RTP etc.
end note

UE <-> gNB: Radio user traffic
gNB <-> UPF: N3: GTP-U Tunnel\n(User Plane packets)
UPF <-> DN: N6: IP traffic to Internet

note bottom
N2 = gNB <-> AMF (Control Plane)
N3 = gNB <-> UPF (User Plane)
N4 = SMF <-> UPF (Rules & forwarding configuration)
N6 = UPF <-> Internet (Data Network)
end note
@enduml


' ------------------------------------------------------------
' Diagram 3: End-to-End 5G Registration + 5G-AKA + PDU Session
' ------------------------------------------------------------
@startuml 5G_E2E_Registration_AKA_PDU
title 5G Registration + 5G-AKA + PDU Session Establishment (End-to-End)

actor UE
participant gNB
participant AMF
participant AUSF
participant "UDM/ARPF\n(Home Network)" as UDM
participant NRF
participant SMF
participant PCF
participant UPF
participant "DN\n(Internet)" as DN

== (A) UE Registration ==
UE -> gNB: RRC Setup Request
gNB -> UE: RRC Setup
UE -> gNB: RRC Setup Complete\n(NAS: Registration Request)
gNB -> AMF: N2 Initial UE Message\n(NAS Registration Request)

note right of AMF
AMF is control-plane entry point.
Handles NAS, mobility, orchestration.
end note

== (B) NF Discovery (SBA Style) ==
AMF -> NRF: Discover AUSF service\n(Nnrf_NFDiscovery)
NRF --> AMF: AUSF endpoint details

== (C) 5G-AKA Authentication ==
AMF -> AUSF: Authenticate UE\n(Nausf_UEAuthentication)

AUSF -> NRF: Discover UDM service
NRF --> AUSF: UDM endpoint details

AUSF -> UDM: Get Authentication Vector\n(Nudm_UEAuthentication_Get)
UDM --> AUSF: AV: RAND, AUTN, XRES*, K_AUSF

AUSF -> AUSF: Derive HXRES*\n& K_SEAF (anchor key)
AUSF --> AMF: Auth Challenge (RAND, AUTN)\n+ HXRES*

AMF --> UE: NAS Authentication Request\n(RAND, AUTN)
UE -> UE: Verify AUTN (network authenticity)
UE -> UE: Compute RES* using USIM secret K
UE --> AMF: NAS Authentication Response\n(RES*)

AMF -> AUSF: Verify RES*
AUSF -> AUSF: Compute HRES* from RES*\nCompare with HXRES*
AUSF --> AMF: Auth Result = SUCCESS\n(K_SEAF / key material)

== (D) Security Mode ==
AMF -> AMF: Derive NAS keys from K_SEAF
AMF --> UE: NAS Security Mode Command\n(Integrity/Ciphering)
UE --> AMF: NAS Security Mode Complete

== (E) Registration Complete ==
AMF --> UE: Registration Accept
UE --> AMF: Registration Complete

== (F) PDU Session Establishment (Internet Session) ==
UE --> AMF: NAS PDU Session Establishment Request\n(DNN, S-NSSAI, Session ID)

AMF -> NRF: Discover SMF service\n(slice/DNN aware)
NRF --> AMF: SMF endpoint details

AMF --> SMF: Create PDU Session\n(Nsmf_PDUSession_CreateSMContext)

SMF -> NRF: Discover PCF service
NRF --> SMF: PCF endpoint details
SMF -> PCF: Get Session Policy/QoS rules\n(Npcf_SMPolicyControl)
PCF --> SMF: QoS/Policy decision

SMF -> NRF: Discover UPF (optional)\n(Nnrf_NFDiscovery)
NRF --> SMF: UPF endpoint details

SMF -> UPF: Establish N4 Session\n(PDR/FAR/QER rules)
UPF --> SMF: N4 Session OK

SMF --> AMF: PDU Session Accepted\n+ N2 SM Info + N3 info
AMF --> gNB: N2 PDU Session Resource Setup Request\n(N2 SM info)
gNB -> gNB: Setup DRB/QoS flows\n(map QFI->DRB)
gNB --> AMF: Resource Setup Response

AMF --> UE: PDU Session Establishment Accept\n(IP info / QoS rules)

== (G) User Plane Data ==
UE <-> gNB: User Data (N3)
gNB <-> UPF: GTP-U tunnel (N3)
UPF <-> DN: N6 traffic (Internet)

note bottom
After this:
- UE has IP
- UPF forwards packets
- QoS flows are active
end note
@enduml

@enduml
